# Keeps the index clean. Not a boundary — see .cursorignore for that.
#
# Everything below stays fully readable by Agent, Tab, and @-mention. All this
# does is stop semantic search handing back spec dumps and generated
# boilerplate when you asked about our code.
#
# Short file, on purpose. .gitignore already drops the generated SQL schema
# snapshots at line 304, about 15.4 MB of them, and Cursor ships a default list
# of roughly a hundred patterns covering lock files, .env*, media, node_modules
# and so on. Between the two, most of the noise is gone before this file is
# even read. Check whether something's already handled before adding it here.
#
# Roughly 18 MB comes out of the index below.
# The full HL7 spec search-parameter bundles, one per FHIR version — 9.2 MB
# between them. This is spec text, not our code, and it buries the actual
# search-parameter handling logic in every search result.
src/Microsoft.Health.Fhir.Core/Data/R4/search-parameters.json
src/Microsoft.Health.Fhir.Core/Data/R4B/search-parameters.json
src/Microsoft.Health.Fhir.Core/Data/R5/search-parameters.json
src/Microsoft.Health.Fhir.Core/Data/Stu3/search-parameters.json

# Implementation Guide profiles and examples, 8.6 MB of vendored spec fixtures
# with no server logic in them. Note this only touches *.json — there are nine
# .http files living inside these same directories and those are real API
# examples worth searching for.
docs/rest/PayerDataExchange/**/*.json
docs/rest/C4BB/**/*.json
docs/rest/DaVinciPlanNet/**/*.json
docs/rest/DaVinciFormulary/**/*.json
docs/rest/Inferno/*.json

# Generated POCOs for the data synth tool. Regenerated from templates, never
# hand-edited, so there's no design intent in them worth surfacing.
tools/FHIRDataSynth/**/*.generated.cs

# Still indexed on purpose — these are calls, not omissions:
#
#   docs/rest/**/*.http (38)       Executable API examples. The thing a
#                                  developer actually goes looking for.
#   ms-search-parameters.json      Microsoft-authored, a few KB. Real
#   BaseCapabilities.json          convention, not spec noise.
#   Data/OperationDefinition/      Hand-authored operation contracts. Small,
#                                  high signal.
#   build/, build/jobs/            DevOps reads this repo too. CI config has
#                                  to stay findable.
#   Schema/Sql/                    Hand-authored sprocs, tables and types —
#                                  the actual schema design.
#   Migrations/*.diff.sql          The record of how each schema change was
#                                  made, one version at a time.
#   TestFiles/ non-patient         QA finds these by searching. The PHI-named
#                                  ones are gone, but that's an access call in
#                                  .cursorignore, not an indexing one.
#   docs/*.md                      Where these rules were mined from in the
#                                  first place.